FocusLoop — Project Description

FocusLoop is an adaptive productivity web application designed to help users understand and reduce procrastination. Instead of providing generic productivity advice, it learns from the user's goals, tasks, behavior patterns, and contextual data to identify what affects their ability to start and complete tasks.

The system follows a continuous loop:

Set Goal → Track Tasks → Collect Behavioral Data → Identify Patterns → Generate AI Insight → Run Personalized Experiment → Measure Results → Improve

Users can create and complete tasks, record procrastination episodes, and view behavioral metrics such as task completion and start delays. The Behavior Engine analyzes this data and provides structured context to an AI system, which explains observed patterns and suggests small, personalized experiments.

The main objective is to move beyond simple productivity tracking and help users discover what actually works for them through evidence-based, measurable behavioral experiments.